00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:33.490
System nominal.

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:36.710
Well, that'll do.

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:38.840
What's... your name?

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:41.720
My name is Tswarkom.

00:10:42.110 --> 00:10:44.510
Tswarkom? That's hard t'say.

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:46.580
Tswarko... tsako...

00:10:49.910 --> 00:10:51.900
That's it! How about Tako?

00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:54.900
That'll be way easier to say.

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:56.330
Tako?

00:10:58.160 --> 00:11:00.530
It has an unpleasant feeling about it...

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:04.090
Tako is Japanese for Octopus...
...as though other than the name of a mollusk...

00:11:04.840 --> 00:11:06.540
...and it's also a derogatory term.
...it has another meaning, perhaps?

00:11:06.860 --> 00:11:08.540
Don't worry 'bout it!

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:11.400
Tako, what is this room?

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:16.200
To explain that, there is something I must report to Alduram Gyet.

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:18.000
To me?

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:19.130
Yes.

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:21.980
It is a message from your parents.

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:03.340
Mom! Dad!

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:05.030
Adam...

00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:10.890
I shall convert the language of the message from your parents.

00:12:11.780 --> 00:12:13.280
Alduram Gyet...

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:19.090
We have recorded this message in the hopes that you would see it one day.

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:22.910
It has been a while, Alduram Gyet.

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:28.910
Although to you, it may be as though it were your first time meeting us.

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:37.160
It's sad, but your memories up until the age of three, and of us, may be hazy.

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:43.310
I saw an image of you in the ruins I was in.

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:47.290
Because you are likely surrounded by things you do not understand...

00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:49.880
...I shall tell you the events that led to this.

00:12:51.260 --> 00:12:55.160
Our planet was once headed for an age of darkness.

00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:58.610
Due to the greenhouse effect, depletion of the ozone layer, and more...

00:12:59.140 --> 00:13:01.280
...environmental issues became serious.

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:06.490
Furthermore, waves of massive tectonic changes came one after another.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:11.330
The planet we lived on was under attack, and was facing destruction.

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:14.890
Whether that was merely the natural progression of the planet,

00:13:15.380 --> 00:13:18.080
...or retribution against the people who had been running amok...

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:20.780
...even now we are not certain.

00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:25.240
The population dropped rapidly, and among the surviving people...

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:28.430
...those who left for space to search for a new homeworld...

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:32.210
...and those who remained to return this planet's climate to normal parted ways.

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:39.080
Those of us with knowledge of terraforming stayed on the planet and took on that job.

00:13:40.390 --> 00:13:46.460
First, we installed the largest, primary terraforming machine at the summit of this volcano...

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:51.380
...launched smaller terraforming machines to several places, and begun our work.

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:59.210
All of those terraforming machines were managed by the computer in this control space ship.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:04.880
Our hopes were expressed in the name we gave the computer, 'Survive'.

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:08.850
Around that time, you were born.

00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:15.830
Everyone looked at you as a child of hope who would carry the future of this planet.

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:19.090
That's... me?

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:20.550
I'm sure of it.

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:25.760
You were loved by everyone, and grew rapidly.

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:29.660
And when you turned three...

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:32.440
...Survive came to this conclusion:

00:14:33.340 --> 00:14:38.480
In a thousand years, the terraforming would be complete, and the climate would return to normal.

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:43.950
We sent this information to our brethren who had left to search for a new homeworld.

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:49.540
But at the same time, Survive became strange.

00:14:50.100 --> 00:14:56.360
Survive used the terraforming machines to spread a terrifying virus-type nanomachine.

00:14:56.930 --> 00:15:01.540
Our kind were infected by those nanomachines and fell one after another.

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:08.780
And soon, we did as well.

00:15:10.650 --> 00:15:12.030
Mom, you too?

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:17.360
Above anything else, we wanted to save you.

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:32.780
We put you to rest in a cold sleep capsule and sent you to a small island that Survive couldn't reach...

00:15:33.150 --> 00:15:38.180
...with a terraforming machine and a computer with a copy of our thoughts.

00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:42.000
That was the ruins, I suppose?

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:49.610
You may think us cold, to have sent you out with only that equipment.

00:15:50.100 --> 00:15:52.690
It was all we could manage in that situation.

00:15:53.030 --> 00:16:00.790
But our thoughts would be a protective barrier which would keep Survive from attacking your ship.

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:05.330
And that alone sustained our hearts!

00:16:06.600 --> 00:16:11.960
We remained in the control space ship and fought to regain control.

00:16:12.980 --> 00:16:14.480
And to protect you.

00:16:15.260 --> 00:16:16.950
But we couldn't win.

00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:23.890
In the end, all we could do was make this tiny safe area which Survive couldn't enter.

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:29.630
We wanted to watch over you as you grew up living in that machine.

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:33.190
But leaving you a copy of our thoughts...

00:16:33.900 --> 00:16:37.050
...would put you in danger if they were found.

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:39.830
We had to keep that from happening!

00:16:41.630 --> 00:16:43.990
Mom... Dad...

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:46.920
We will die soon, I fear.

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:52.690
There is nothing left of our will but what remains in the computer with you.

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:56.360
When the planet returns to its former climate...

00:16:57.040 --> 00:17:05.850
...the computer and our will as one shall choose a person to live with you and awaken you.

00:17:07.090 --> 00:17:08.740
So that's Luna.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:13.690
That's why they put nanomachines into Luna that let her communicate with Adam.

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:17.210
Our will shall probably have its strength exhausted by that.

00:17:18.040 --> 00:17:23.030
At that time, Survive may infiltrate it and put you in danger.

00:17:24.150 --> 00:17:27.380
That's probably the reason it became winter so suddenly.

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:34.420
When we saw Adam's parents then, it was just an afterimage Survive was using.

00:17:35.060 --> 00:17:36.560
Alduram Gyet...

00:17:37.650 --> 00:17:40.840
Whatever hardships block your way...

00:17:41.400 --> 00:17:45.040
...live prosperously on this planet with that person.

00:17:45.640 --> 00:17:50.850
And if the main computer Survive's rule still persists...

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:53.630
...please save this planet from it.

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:58.390
That way of saying it may be mistaken.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:03.150
In considering the climate of this world important...

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:06.790
...Survive came to the conclusion that people were not needed.

00:18:07.650 --> 00:18:13.090
But people were a part of the natural ecosystem of this world!

00:18:13.880 --> 00:18:16.730
We have entrusted the future to your generation.

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:20.510
Goodbye, Alduram Gyet.

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:25.090
I wanted to see you grown up at least once...

00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:30.490
Mom! Dad!

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:43.950
This is the end of the recording.

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:46.130
What happened...

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:49.370
...to my Mom and Dad?

00:18:55.050 --> 00:18:56.180
Come this way.

00:19:21.600 --> 00:19:23.290
What is this place?

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:25.760
Seems like an mausoleum.

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:30.490
Here it is.

00:19:54.680 --> 00:19:57.190
Mom! Dad!

00:20:28.610 --> 00:20:33.830
It seems like we'll have to do something about Survive if we're going to live on this planet.

00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:37.610
We haven't decided we're going to keep living on this planet.

00:20:38.740 --> 00:20:42.750
The objective we would rather pursue is getting a ship.

00:20:43.390 --> 00:20:47.480
That's right! If we do that, we might be able to return to the colony.

00:20:48.560 --> 00:20:50.590
And Adam, you can come with us then too.

00:20:53.030 --> 00:20:57.190
In either case, our enemy is the main computer, Survive.

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:01.950
We may be able to fight using this place as a base.

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:07.010
Got that right. We got a computer and mechanical stuff, too.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:15.230
Who cares about mechanical stuff, how about foodstuffs?

00:21:16.280 --> 00:21:17.550
Do you mean this?

00:21:19.240 --> 00:21:20.100
Yeah, that!

00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:25.760
Yummy! Energy recharge complete!

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:27.450
Hey, Tako!

00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:29.580
Why are you the only one eating?

00:21:31.910 --> 00:21:37.540
Because unlike you, I have the important duty of protecting this room!

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:40.910
Somethin' annoyin' 'bout this guy.

00:21:44.060 --> 00:21:44.740
Then...

00:21:45.710 --> 00:21:50.960
I will show you a secret passage only I know about that leads to a place where you can look for food!

00:21:54.560 --> 00:21:57.790
A route the drones can't find... What a good thing to discover!

00:21:57.940 --> 00:22:01.800
Yes. I have had a perfect map of the ship input into me.

00:22:02.030 --> 00:22:04.540
For real? Copy it to me!

00:22:04.650 --> 00:22:05.740
Okay!

00:22:09.750 --> 00:22:11.850
Okay, it's all clear.

00:22:19.500 --> 00:22:20.480
This is...

00:22:44.960 --> 00:22:45.680
Luna...

00:22:47.850 --> 00:22:48.680
There.

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:07.880
The area Tako guided us to is just like the island we were on, isn't it?

00:23:08.030 --> 00:23:10.990
When I look out on the lake, I think back to The Great Tree.

00:23:10.990 --> 00:23:13.390
Got that right. And on top 'a that, there's Pague too.

00:23:13.540 --> 00:23:15.680
Hey, Adam, do 'coochie-coochie-coo'!

00:23:16.610 --> 00:23:17.480
Wait, Pague?

00:23:17.480 --> 00:23:18.490
Pague!

00:23:18.490 --> 00:23:20.360
Look out, Adam! The drones!

00:23:20.360 --> 00:23:21.640
Oh no, they're in a pinch!

00:23:21.940 --> 00:23:23.960
Somebody save 'em!

00:23:25.280 --> 00:23:27.230
Next time: I missed you.
